IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc11-evidence`

-- evidence: tests of ccc11-evidence.l4 (Part VIII.1, sections 320.31 to 320.35: evidentiary matters)
-- Expected values are written by hand from the text of the provision, beside each assertion, before the run; none is copied from the code's output.
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING: the text says yes / the text says no in its own words / not covered.

GIVEN l IS A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 320.34 test: the number of items` MEANS
    CONSIDER l
    WHEN JUST items THEN JUST (sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD 1) items))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§ `s 320.31(1): breath results are conclusive proof if the instrument, the technician, the blank test (not more than 10 mg), the calibration check (within 10% of the target), the 15-minute interval and the rounding rule (not more than 20 mg apart) all hold`
-- arguments: approved instrument (by s 320.11) ; qualified technician (by s 320.11) ; blank test result ; calibration check result ; target value ; standard certified by an analyst (by s 320.11) ; interval in minutes ; first result ; second result
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 10 100 100 (JUST TRUE) 15 90 100 EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- every condition met, each at its limit
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 11 100 100 (JUST TRUE) 15 90 100 EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- blank test over 10 mg
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 0 90 100 (JUST TRUE) 15 90 100 EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- calibration check exactly 10% below the target
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 0 89.9 100 (JUST TRUE) 15 90 100 EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- calibration check more than 10% below the target
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 0 110 100 (JUST TRUE) 15 90 100 EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- calibration check exactly 10% above the target
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 0 110.1 100 (JUST TRUE) 15 90 100 EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- calibration check more than 10% above the target
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 0 100 100 (JUST TRUE) 14 90 100 EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- an interval of 14 minutes is under 15
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 0 100 100 (JUST TRUE) 15 89 109 EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- rounded down 80 and 100 differ by exactly 20: not "more than 20"
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 0 100 100 (JUST TRUE) 15 89 110 EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- rounded down 80 and 110 differ by 30
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 0 100 100 (JUST TRUE) 15 109 89 EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- the same pair in the other order
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 0 100 100 (JUST TRUE) 15 110 89 EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the same pair in the other order
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 0 100 100 (JUST TRUE) 15 100 100 EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- results the same
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) 0 100 100 (JUST TRUE) 15 90 100 EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not an approved instrument: the "if" is unmet
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) 0 100 100 (JUST TRUE) 15 90 100 EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether it is an approved instrument is not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING 0 100 100 (JUST TRUE) 15 90 100 EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether the operator is a qualified technician is not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) 0 100 100 (JUST TRUE) 15 90 100 EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not a qualified technician
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 0 100 100 (JUST FALSE) 15 90 100 EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the alcohol standard is not certified by an analyst
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) 0 100 100 NOTHING 15 90 100 EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether the analyst certified it is not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the results of the analyses of the breath samples are conclusive proof of the person’s blood alcohol concentration` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) 20 100 100 (JUST TRUE) 15 90 100 EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- a numeric condition fails: a no beats a not-covered
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the blood alcohol concentration that the results are conclusive proof of, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` (JUST TRUE) 90 100 EQUALS JUST 90   -- the lowest of different results
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the blood alcohol concentration that the results are conclusive proof of, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` (JUST TRUE) 100 90 EQUALS JUST 90   -- the lowest, other order
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the blood alcohol concentration that the results are conclusive proof of, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` (JUST TRUE) 95 95 EQUALS JUST 95   -- the results are the same
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the blood alcohol concentration that the results are conclusive proof of, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` (JUST FALSE) 90 100 EQUALS NOTHING   -- conditions not met: the results prove nothing under this subsection
#ASSERT `s 320.31(1) the blood alcohol concentration that the results are conclusive proof of, in mg of alcohol in 100 mL of blood` NOTHING 90 100 EQUALS NOTHING   -- conditions not covered

§ `s 320.31(2) and (3): blood analysis is proof in the absence of evidence of improper analysis; three kinds of evidence are not such evidence`
-- arguments for (2): made by an analyst (by s 320.11) ; there is evidence tending to show improper analysis
#ASSERT `s 320.31(2) the result of the analysis of the blood sample is proof of the person’s concentration at the time the sample was taken` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an analyst, no such evidence
#ASSERT `s 320.31(2) the result of the analysis of the blood sample is proof of the person’s concentration at the time the sample was taken` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- evidence tending to show improper analysis: "in the absence of"
#ASSERT `s 320.31(2) the result of the analysis of the blood sample is proof of the person’s concentration at the time the sample was taken` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not made by an analyst
#ASSERT `s 320.31(2) the result of the analysis of the blood sample is proof of the person’s concentration at the time the sample was taken` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether it was made by an analyst is not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.31(3) the evidence constitutes evidence tending to show that the analysis of the blood sample was performed improperly` `s 320.31(3)(a) evidence of the amount of alcohol or a drug that they consumed` EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 320.31(3) the evidence constitutes evidence tending to show that the analysis of the blood sample was performed improperly` `s 320.31(3)(b) evidence of the rate at which the alcohol or the drug would have been absorbed or eliminated by their body` EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 320.31(3) the evidence constitutes evidence tending to show that the analysis of the blood sample was performed improperly` `s 320.31(3)(c) a calculation based on the evidence referred to in paragraphs (a) and (b) of what their blood alcohol concentration or blood drug concentration would have been at the time the sample was taken` EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 320.31(3) the evidence constitutes evidence tending to show that the analysis of the blood sample was performed improperly` `s 320.31(3) evidence of any other kind` EQUALS NOTHING   -- any other evidence is not addressed

§ `s 320.31(4): the presumption for samples taken more than two hours after, with a concentration of at least 20 mg: add 5 mg for every complete 30 minutes beyond two hours (fork F14)`
-- arguments: minutes after ceasing to operate at which the first breath sample, or the blood sample, was taken ; the concentration established under (1) or (2)
#ASSERT `s 320.31(4) the blood alcohol concentration within the two hours after the person ceased to operate the conveyance is conclusively presumed to be` 120 100 EQUALS NOTHING   -- exactly two hours: not "more than two hours"
#ASSERT `s 320.31(4) the blood alcohol concentration within the two hours after the person ceased to operate the conveyance is conclusively presumed to be` 121 100 EQUALS JUST 100   -- one minute over: no complete interval of 30 minutes yet
#ASSERT `s 320.31(4) the blood alcohol concentration within the two hours after the person ceased to operate the conveyance is conclusively presumed to be` 149 100 EQUALS JUST 100   -- 29 minutes over
#ASSERT `s 320.31(4) the blood alcohol concentration within the two hours after the person ceased to operate the conveyance is conclusively presumed to be` 150 100 EQUALS JUST 105   -- one complete interval
#ASSERT `s 320.31(4) the blood alcohol concentration within the two hours after the person ceased to operate the conveyance is conclusively presumed to be` 179 100 EQUALS JUST 105   -- 59 minutes over: one complete interval
#ASSERT `s 320.31(4) the blood alcohol concentration within the two hours after the person ceased to operate the conveyance is conclusively presumed to be` 180 100 EQUALS JUST 110   -- two complete intervals
#ASSERT `s 320.31(4) the blood alcohol concentration within the two hours after the person ceased to operate the conveyance is conclusively presumed to be` 210 50 EQUALS JUST 65   -- three complete intervals
#ASSERT `s 320.31(4) the blood alcohol concentration within the two hours after the person ceased to operate the conveyance is conclusively presumed to be` 150 20 EQUALS JUST 25   -- the concentration is exactly 20: "equal to or exceeded 20"
#ASSERT `s 320.31(4) the blood alcohol concentration within the two hours after the person ceased to operate the conveyance is conclusively presumed to be` 150 19.9 EQUALS NOTHING   -- under 20 mg: the presumption does not apply

§ `s 320.31(5) to (10): admissibility, presumptions about a drug, failure to provide a sample`
#ASSERT `s 320.31(5) the evaluating officer’s opinion is admissible in evidence without qualifying the evaluating officer as an expert` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- an evaluating officer's opinion on impairment by an identified drug
#ASSERT `s 320.31(5) the evaluating officer’s opinion is admissible in evidence without qualifying the evaluating officer as an expert` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not about impairment by an identified drug: not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.31(5) the evaluating officer’s opinion is admissible in evidence without qualifying the evaluating officer as an expert` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- evaluating officer status not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.31(5) the evaluating officer’s opinion is admissible in evidence without qualifying the evaluating officer as an expert` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an evaluating officer
-- arguments for (6): the analysis demonstrates the drug the officer identified ; evidence to the contrary
#ASSERT `s 320.31(6) the drug, or the combination, is presumed to have been present in the person’s body at the time when the person operated the conveyance` TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- presumed present at the time
#ASSERT `s 320.31(6) the drug, or the combination, is presumed to have been present in the person’s body at the time when the person operated the conveyance` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- "in the absence of evidence to the contrary"
#ASSERT `s 320.31(6) the drug, or the combination, is presumed to have been present in the person’s body at the time when the person operated the conveyance` FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the "if" is unmet
-- arguments for the cause presumption: the analysis demonstrates ; the impairment is proved ; evidence to the contrary
#ASSERT `s 320.31(6) the drug, or the combination, is presumed to have been the cause of the person’s impairment` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- on proof of impairment, presumed the cause
#ASSERT `s 320.31(6) the drug, or the combination, is presumed to have been the cause of the person’s impairment` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- impairment not proved
#ASSERT `s 320.31(6) the drug, or the combination, is presumed to have been the cause of the person’s impairment` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- evidence to the contrary
#ASSERT `s 320.31(6) the drug, or the combination, is presumed to have been the cause of the person’s impairment` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the analysis does not demonstrate the drug
#ASSERT `s 320.31(7) the result of the analysis may be admitted in evidence even if the person was not warned` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a sample the person was not required to provide may be admitted even if no warning was given
#ASSERT `s 320.31(7) the result of the analysis may be admitted in evidence even if the person was not warned` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a sample they were required to provide: the subsection does not speak
#ASSERT `s 320.31(8) evidence that the person failed or refused to provide a sample, or that a sample was not taken, is not admissible` FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- not required to provide a sample: the evidence is not admissible
#ASSERT `s 320.31(8) evidence that the person failed or refused to provide a sample, or that a sample was not taken, is not admissible` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- required: the "unless" is met and the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `s 320.31(8) the failure, refusal or fact that a sample was not taken shall not be the subject of comment by any person in any proceedings under this Part` FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- not required: the failure shall not be the subject of comment
#ASSERT `s 320.31(8) the failure, refusal or fact that a sample was not taken shall not be the subject of comment by any person in any proceedings under this Part` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- required: the "unless" is met
#ASSERT `s 320.31(9) the statement is admissible in evidence for the purpose of justifying a demand` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- made to a peace officer, offered to justify a demand
#ASSERT `s 320.31(9) the statement is admissible in evidence for the purpose of justifying a demand` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- offered for another purpose: not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.31(9) the statement is admissible in evidence for the purpose of justifying a demand` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not made to a peace officer
#ASSERT `s 320.31(9) the statement is admissible in evidence for the purpose of justifying a demand` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- peace officer status not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.31(10) the evidence of the failure or refusal to comply with the demand is admissible` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- proceedings under 320.14, a failure or refusal without reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `s 320.31(10) the evidence of the failure or refusal to comply with the demand is admissible` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not proceedings under 320.14
#ASSERT `s 320.31(10) the evidence of the failure or refusal to comply with the demand is admissible` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- other evidence
#ASSERT `s 320.31(10) the court may draw an inference adverse to the accused from the evidence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- the court may draw an adverse inference
#ASSERT `s 320.31(10) the court may draw an inference adverse to the accused from the evidence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 320.31(10) the court may draw an inference adverse to the accused from the evidence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING; the sweep lists the "in any proceedings in respect of" gate of the inference with the guide's JUST FALSE outside proceedings under 320.14 (fork F36)
#ASSERT `s 320.31(10) the court may draw an inference adverse to the accused from the evidence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not proceedings under 320.14, other evidence: a no beats a not-covered
#ASSERT `s 320.31(10) the court may draw an inference adverse to the accused from the evidence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- other evidence

§ `s 320.32: certificates (evidence without proof of signature; notice and copy; attendance; the 30-day rules; certificates of prohibition; the onus after mailing)`
#ASSERT `s 320.32(1) the certificate is evidence of the facts alleged in it without proof of the signature or the official character of the person who signed it` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a certificate of an analyst, practitioner or technician made under this Part
#ASSERT `s 320.32(1) the certificate is evidence of the facts alleged in it without proof of the signature or the official character of the person who signed it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another kind of certificate: not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.32(2) the certificate is barred from being received in evidence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- notice and copy given before the trial: not barred by this subsection
#ASSERT `s 320.32(2) the certificate is barred from being received in evidence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- no notice: barred
#ASSERT `s 320.32(2) the certificate is barred from being received in evidence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- no copy: barred
#ASSERT `s 320.32(2) the certificate is barred from being received in evidence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- neither: barred
#ASSERT `s 320.32(3) the party may apply to the court for an order requiring the attendance of the person who signed the certificate for cross-examination` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a party against whom the certificate is produced may apply
#ASSERT `s 320.32(3) the party may apply to the court for an order requiring the attendance of the person who signed the certificate for cross-examination` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not such a party: not covered
-- arguments for (4): in writing ; sets out the likely relevance ; the day a copy was given to the prosecutor ; the day the application is to be heard
#ASSERT `s 320.32(4) the application meets the requirements of form, content and notice` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- a copy given exactly 30 days before the hearing
#ASSERT `s 320.32(4) the application meets the requirements of form, content and notice` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- 29 days before the hearing
#ASSERT `s 320.32(4) the application meets the requirements of form, content and notice` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- 31 days before
#ASSERT `s 320.32(4) the application meets the requirements of form, content and notice` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not in writing
#ASSERT `s 320.32(4) the application meets the requirements of form, content and notice` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- does not set out the likely relevance
-- arguments for (5): the day the hearing is held ; the day the trial is to be held
#ASSERT `s 320.32(5) the hearing of the application is held at least 30 days before the day on which the trial is to be held` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- exactly 30 days before the trial
#ASSERT `s 320.32(5) the hearing of the application is held at least 30 days before the day on which the trial is to be held` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- 29 days before the trial
#ASSERT `s 320.32(5) the hearing of the application is held at least 30 days before the day on which the trial is to be held` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 31 3 2027) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- 30 days, in a year with the same calendar
-- arguments for (6)(a): the proceedings are for an offence under 320.18(1) ; the certificate says the person is prohibited from operating a motor vehicle in the province ; signed by the registrar of motor vehicles or a person authorized
#ASSERT `s 320.32(6)(a) the certificate is evidence of the facts alleged in it without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed it` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- all three
#ASSERT `s 320.32(6)(a) the certificate is evidence of the facts alleged in it without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed it` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not proceedings for an offence under 320.18(1)
#ASSERT `s 320.32(6)(a) the certificate is evidence of the facts alleged in it without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed it` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a certificate of that content
#ASSERT `s 320.32(6)(a) the certificate is evidence of the facts alleged in it without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed it` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- signed by someone else
#ASSERT `s 320.32(6)(b) the certificate is evidence of the facts alleged in it without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed it` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- (b) all three
#ASSERT `s 320.32(6)(b) the certificate is evidence of the facts alleged in it without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed it` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (b) not signed by the Minister of Transport or a person authorized
-- arguments for (7): a prohibition is proved ; notice mailed is proved ; the day the notice was mailed ; the day asked about ; evidence to the contrary
#ASSERT `s 320.32(7) the person is presumed to have received the notice and to have knowledge of the prohibition, of the date of its commencement and of its duration` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- the tenth day after the day of mailing
#ASSERT `s 320.32(7) the person is presumed to have received the notice and to have knowledge of the prohibition, of the date of its commencement and of its duration` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the ninth day: before the period the text fixes
#ASSERT `s 320.32(7) the person is presumed to have received the notice and to have knowledge of the prohibition, of the date of its commencement and of its duration` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- long after
#ASSERT `s 320.32(7) the person is presumed to have received the notice and to have knowledge of the prohibition, of the date of its commencement and of its duration` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- evidence to the contrary
#ASSERT `s 320.32(7) the person is presumed to have received the notice and to have knowledge of the prohibition, of the date of its commencement and of its duration` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the prohibition is not proved
#ASSERT `s 320.32(7) the person is presumed to have received the notice and to have knowledge of the prohibition, of the date of its commencement and of its duration` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the mailing is not proved
#ASSERT `s 320.33 the printout is evidence of the facts alleged in the document without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed it` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- printed out from an approved instrument, signed by a qualified technician who certifies it
#ASSERT `s 320.33 the printout is evidence of the facts alleged in the document without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed it` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the technician does not certify it
#ASSERT `s 320.33 the printout is evidence of the facts alleged in the document without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed it` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not printed from an approved instrument
#ASSERT `s 320.33 the printout is evidence of the facts alleged in the document without proof of the signature or official character of the person who signed it` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- technician status not covered

§ `s 320.34, 320.35: disclosure and the presumption of operation`
#ASSERT `s 320.34(1) the prosecutor shall disclose to the accused information about the breath samples` TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- proceedings under 320.14 and breath samples provided under 320.28
#ASSERT `s 320.34(1) the prosecutor shall disclose to the accused information about the breath samples` FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not proceedings under 320.14
#ASSERT `s 320.34(1) the prosecutor shall disclose to the accused information about the breath samples` TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no breath samples provided under 320.28
#ASSERT `s 320.34 test: the number of items` (`s 320.34(1)(a) to (e) the information the prosecutor shall disclose` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST 5   -- five items, (a) to (e)
#ASSERT `s 320.34 test: the number of items` (`s 320.34(1)(a) to (e) the information the prosecutor shall disclose` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING   -- no duty: not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.34 test: the number of items` (`s 320.34(1)(a) to (e) the information the prosecutor shall disclose` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.34(1) the prosecutor shall disclose information about the breath samples to the accused` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FULFILLED   -- no duty arises
#TRACE `s 320.34(1) the prosecutor shall disclose information about the breath samples to the accused` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 320.34(1) disclose to the accused information sufficient to determine whether the conditions set out in paragraphs 320.31(1)(a) to (c) have been met` AT 1
#ASSERT `s 320.34(2) the accused may apply to the court for a hearing to determine whether further information should be disclosed` TRUE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- proceedings under 320.14: the accused may apply for a hearing
#ASSERT `s 320.34(2) the accused may apply to the court for a hearing to determine whether further information should be disclosed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not covered
#ASSERT `s 320.34(3) the application meets the requirements of form, content and notice` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- in writing, particulars, 30 days
#ASSERT `s 320.34(3) the application meets the requirements of form, content and notice` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- 29 days
#ASSERT `s 320.34(3) the application meets the requirements of form, content and notice` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not in writing
#ASSERT `s 320.34(3) the application meets the requirements of form, content and notice` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- no detailed particulars
#ASSERT `s 320.34(4) the hearing of the application is held at least 30 days before the day on which the trial is to be held` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- exactly 30 days before the trial
#ASSERT `s 320.34(4) the hearing of the application is held at least 30 days before the day on which the trial is to be held` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- 29 days
#ASSERT `s 320.34(5) section 320.34 limits the disclosure to which the accused may otherwise be entitled` TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- "nothing in this section limits the disclosure to which the accused may otherwise be entitled"
#ASSERT `s 320.34(5) section 320.34 limits the disclosure to which the accused may otherwise be entitled` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no such other disclosure: the subsection is silent
#ASSERT `s 320.35 the accused is presumed to have been operating the conveyance` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)   -- occupied the driver's seat: presumed to have been operating
#ASSERT `s 320.35 the accused is presumed to have been operating the conveyance` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- the accused establishes that they did not occupy the seat to set the conveyance in motion
#ASSERT `s 320.35 the accused is presumed to have been operating the conveyance` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not proceedings under 320.14 or 320.15
#ASSERT `s 320.35 the accused is presumed to have been operating the conveyance` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)   -- not proved that the accused occupied that seat

